---
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Legal Notice | einvoiceops</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Legal notice, service scope, content verification standard, and limitation of liability for einvoiceops." />
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    :root {
      --navy:   #1a2b3c;
      --accent: #2563eb;
      --text:   #111827;
      --sub:    #374151;
      --muted:  #6b7280;
      --border: #e5e7eb;
      --bg:     #ffffff;
      --bg-alt: #f8f9fa;
      --sans:   -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
    }
    body {
      font-family: var(--sans);
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--bg);
      line-height: 1.6;
      font-size: 16px;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    }
    main {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 56px 2rem 80px;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: -0.03em;
      color: var(--navy);
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .subtitle {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin-bottom: 48px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 0.78rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.07em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 36px 0 10px;
    }
    h3 {
      font-size: 1rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--navy);
      margin: 28px 0 8px;
    }
    p, address, li {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--sub);
      line-height: 1.75;
      font-style: normal;
    }
    p + p { margin-top: 10px; }
    ul {
      margin: 10px 0 10px 1.4rem;
    }
    li + li { margin-top: 6px; }
    .divider {
      border: none;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      margin: 48px 0;
    }
    .pending {
      color: #92400e;
      font-style: italic;
    }
    .notice {
      background: #eff6ff;
      border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
      border-radius: 6px;
      padding: 14px 18px;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      color: #1e40af;
      line-height: 1.65;
      margin-top: 40px;
    }
    .scope-block {
      background: var(--bg-alt);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 20px 24px;
      margin: 20px 0;
    }
    .scope-block h3 {
      margin-top: 0;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .scope-block ul {
      margin-top: 0;
    }
    .scope-block li {
      font-size: 0.9rem;
    }
    .confidence-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 16px 0;
      font-size: 0.875rem;
    }
    .confidence-table th {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      background: var(--bg-alt);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--navy);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }
    .confidence-table td {
      padding: 10px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      color: var(--sub);
      vertical-align: top;
    }
    .badge-green {
      display: inline-block;
      background: #dcfce7;
      color: #166534;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 2px 7px;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    .badge-amber {
      display: inline-block;
      background: #fef9c3;
      color: #854d0e;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      padding: 2px 7px;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }
    a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
    a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    footer {
      padding: 28px 2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 12px;
    }
    footer p { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); }
    footer a { color: var(--accent); }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <Nav />

  <main>
    <h1>Legal Notice</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">
      Impressum (DE) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Mentions L&eacute;gales (FR) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Palveluntarjoajan tiedot (FI)
    </p>

    <h2>Service Provider</h2>
    <address>
      Nomos Digital Oy (trading as einvoiceops)<br />
      Jens Anttila, Board Member<br />
      Nallenpolku 4 F 90<br />
      02110 Espoo<br />
      Finland
    </address>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Email: <a href="mailto:jens@einvoiceops.eu">jens@einvoiceops.eu</a><br />
      Phone: <a href="tel:+358400374990">+358 400 374 990</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Business Registration</h2>
    <p>
      Finnish Business ID (Y-tunnus): 3621903-9<br />
      VAT Registration Number: <span class="pending">pending</span>
    </p>

    <h2>Regulatory Basis</h2>
    <p>
      This legal notice is provided pursuant to the Finnish Act on Electronic Communications Services
      (917/2014), the EU e-Commerce Directive (2000/31/EC), German teleservices legislation (DDG),
      and French requirements under the Loi pour la Confiance dans l'&Eacute;conomie
      Num&eacute;rique (LCEN 2004-575).
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>What einvoiceops is</h2>

    <p>
      einvoiceops provides operational readiness support for EU e-invoicing mandates. Each EU member
      state legislates e-invoicing independently: different formats, different platform models,
      different identifiers, different deadlines. For organisations with operations across multiple
      EU countries, the practical challenge is not understanding that mandates exist. The challenge
      is translating each mandate's specific technical and operational requirements into concrete
      preparation work, assigned to the right internal owners - IT, tax, finance systems, AP
      operations - before a deadline creates pressure.
    </p>
    <p>
      einvoiceops tracks EU mandate requirements against primary sources (enacted legislation,
      official gazettes, tax authority publications) and translates that information into structured
      operational preparation. The compliance map on this site reflects the current state of each
      country's mandate as verified against those primary sources. Where content is marked as
      source-verified, a specialist confirmed the specific claim matches the primary document on
      the stated date.
    </p>
    <p>
      The paid service goes further: mandate changes are translated into ERP-specific preparation
      work and routed to named internal owners, so that when a deadline arrives, the organisation
      has a traceable preparation record rather than a gap.
    </p>

    <div class="scope-block">
      <h3>In scope</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Mandate tracking: dates, formats, thresholds, compliance parameters per EU country</li>
        <li>Operational preparation: translating mandate requirements into internal work items with named owners</li>
        <li>Readiness assessment: identifying which internal functions are affected by a given mandate</li>
        <li>Change monitoring: detecting when mandate requirements are updated and flagging what needs re-preparation</li>
        <li>Structured delivery: work packets with official source citations, named internal owners, and version history</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>What einvoiceops is not</h2>

    <p>
      einvoiceops is not a law firm, licensed legal advisor, certified tax consultant, or compliance
      authority. No content on this site, and no deliverable produced through the paid service,
      constitutes legal advice, tax advice, or a compliance opinion.
    </p>
    <p>
      Operational preparation is not the same as compliance assurance. einvoiceops helps organisations
      structure the internal work required to prepare for a mandate. Whether that preparation produces
      legal compliance in a specific organisation's circumstances is a determination that requires
      qualified legal and tax counsel with full knowledge of that organisation's entity structure,
      VAT registrations, contracts, and systems. einvoiceops does not make that determination and
      does not represent that its outputs do.
    </p>
    <p>
      The content on this site is mandate intelligence and tracking, not legal interpretation. When
      a law says "invoices must be transmitted within 12 days of the supply date," einvoiceops
      records that requirement and cites the source. It does not interpret whether your organisation's
      specific invoicing practices fall within or outside that requirement. That interpretation
      requires qualified legal or tax advice.
    </p>

    <div class="scope-block">
      <h3>Not in scope - under any circumstances</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Legal interpretation of mandate requirements in the context of your organisation</li>
        <li>Tax advice or VAT opinions</li>
        <li>Compliance certification or sign-off</li>
        <li>Confirmation that your organisation is compliant with any mandate</li>
        <li>Advice on penalty exposure or enforcement risk</li>
        <li>Interpretation of conflicting sources or legislative ambiguity</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>Content Verification Standard</h2>

    <p>
      Mandate content on this site is assigned a confidence tier based on what has been confirmed
      against primary sources. The tiers do not represent legal certainty. They represent the
      current state of source verification.
    </p>

    <table class="confidence-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Tier</th>
          <th>What it means</th>
          <th>What it does not mean</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="badge-green">Green</span></td>
          <td>A specialist verified the specific claim against the primary source document on the stated date.</td>
          <td>Legal confirmation that the claim is correct as a matter of law, or that it applies to your organisation specifically.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><span class="badge-amber">Amber</span></td>
          <td>The claim has a source citation and the source is plausible, but the primary document has not yet been personally confirmed by a specialist. The claim is likely accurate but treated as unconfirmed until that step is complete.</td>
          <td>That the claim should be acted upon without independent validation. Amber claims should be treated as indicative until confirmed.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>What verification means and does not mean</h3>
    <p>
      Verification in the einvoiceops system is claim-source matching: confirming that a specific
      published claim matches what a specific primary source document actually says. This is a
      reading task, not a legal analysis task. The question being answered is: "Does this law
      article say the mandate applies from January 2026?" not "Does this mandate apply to your
      organisation and what does it require of you?"
    </p>
    <p>
      When primary sources conflict on the same claim, the conflict is flagged explicitly and the
      claim is not resolved to a single answer. Resolving legislative ambiguity requires qualified
      legal judgment. einvoiceops does not perform that judgment and does not publish a resolved
      answer in place of an honest flag.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <em>last verified</em> date on each country page records when a specialist last confirmed
      the source content for that country. It is a snapshot date, not a guarantee of current
      accuracy. EU regulatory requirements change. Content may not reflect the most current state
      at the time of reading.
    </p>

    <hr class="divider" />

    <h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>

    <p>
      Content on this site is provided for operational preparation purposes only. einvoiceops (Nomos
      Digital Oy) accepts no liability for decisions taken based on this content without independent
      legal and tax validation. Customers remain responsible for all compliance decisions,
      their implementation, and their legal consequences.
    </p>
    <p>
      EU e-invoicing requirements are subject to ongoing legislative change. einvoiceops makes
      reasonable efforts to track and reflect those changes but does not warrant that content is
      current, complete, or free of error at the time of reading. Users who require current and
      authoritative mandate information for compliance decisions should consult the relevant
      national tax authority publications and qualified legal counsel.
    </p>

    <h2>Governing Law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by Finnish law. Disputes are subject to the jurisdiction of Finnish
      courts, specifically the District Court of Espoo (Espoon käräjäoikeus) as the court of first
      instance, unless mandatory EU consumer protection rules require otherwise.
    </p>

  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>einvoiceops &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="mailto:jens@einvoiceops.eu">jens@einvoiceops.eu</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Finland</p>
    <p>&copy; 2026 einvoiceops &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="/legal/">Legal Notice</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
